{
  "name": "_shootoutOrderMenu",
  "comment": "PENALTY SHOOTOUT's SHOOTING ORDER screen (src/penalty_shootout.c), shown by ShowPlayMatchMenu in place of the PLAY MATCH screen while the mode is on: a match that is only penalties has no use for tactics, squad swaps or substitutes, so the one choice is who shoots when. The ten outfield players are the queue, positions 1..5 (the best-of-five takers) a gap above 6..10; click a player and then another and they trade places (ShootoutOrderRowSelected). Rows render through the ViewSquad pattern: the row template's after_draw (ShootoutOrderRowDraw) builds the 12-entry BuildTransferPlayerMenuEntry bank at the end of the stream. START SHOOTOUT keeps PlayMatchSelected's contract (which pad pressed it becomes playerNumThatStarted), EXIT is the abort. Both targets: a classic packed menu, so the m68k build gets it from the baked src/menu_data.c.",
  "onInit": "ShootoutOrderMenuInit",
  "onReturn": "ShootoutOrderMenuInit",
  "onDraw": null,
